Despite significant challenges in the national economy, particularly during the 2020–2023 period when the economy suffered severely from the COVID-19 pandemic. With decisive direction from the National Assembly, the Government, and the Prime Minister, the Ministry of Construction worked closely with the State Bank of Vietnam and other ministries, sectors, and local authorities to implement concessional loan support programs.
These programs targeted beneficiaries of social housing policies, enterprises, and cooperatives involved in social housing construction, as well as other housing support initiatives through national target programs and public investment housing programs. Many localities allocated land funds for social housing development, ensuring alignment with technical and social infrastructure systems to meet the needs of low-income individuals, workers, and laborers in industrial zones.

Despite the achieved results, the legal framework on social housing effective during the 2015–2023 period still lacked stability. Certain legal provisions on social housing development lacked specific guidance;

