source:
1. An application for issuance of copies from a master register shall include the following:
a) One of the following documents: Unexpired e-ID card; the original or a copy of the unexpired Citizen ID Card, unexpired ID Card, unexpired ID Certificate, unexpired Passport, unexpired travel document or an unexpired international laissez-passer;

b) The original or a certified true copy of documents proving the relationship with the person to whom the original is issued, in cases specified in clauses 2 and 3 of Article 16 of this Decree.

2. Procedures for obtaining copies from the master register:

a) In the case of submitting the application directly to the competent agency or organization, the applicant shall present the documents prescribed in Clause 1 of this Article for the receiving person to verify;

b) In the case of submitting the application by post, the applicant must enclose the documents prescribed in Clause 1 of this Article along with one stamped envelope clearly indicating the name and address of the recipient;

c) In the case of submitting the application online, the applicant may submit the electronic document specified in Clause 1 of this Article or its electronic copy.

3. The agency or organization shall issue copies based on the master register; contents of copies must accurately reflect the original register. In cases where the master register is no longer stored or does not contain the requested information, the agency or organization is responsible for responding in writing to the requester.

The results shall be delivered in person, by post or online according to the method registered by the requester.

4. The period for issuing a copy from the master register shall comply with the provisions of Article 7 of this Decree. The period shall begin from the date the agency or organization receives a satisfactory application in person, from the date of receipt written in the postmark or from the date as recorded by the public service system as “satisfactory application received”.

