3. Form and duration of training:

a) Training program for laws regarding rights to plant varieties shall be conducted in one of the following forms:
in person; online; combination of in person and online. The form of training shall be decided by training institutions in accordance with actual conditions and training quality.

b) The theoretical content of the training program shall not exceed 70% while practical exercises and discussions shall be at least 30%.

c) Duration of training: 05 days, at least 40 periods.

4. Instructors
a) Instructors teaching legislative documents regarding plant variety protection shall hold at least a university degree, have a minimum of 05 years of experience in plant variety protection, possess knowledge of laws on plant variety protection, or have participated in the development of legislative documents on plant variety protection.

