Article 20. Requesting foreign countries to provide criminal legal assistance

1. Presiding authorities in Vietnam, in the course of criminal proceedings, may request overseas competent authorities to provide legal assistance in the following cases:

a) Service of papers and documents on persons who are residing in the requested countries;

b/ Summon of witness and experts who are living in the requested countries;
c) Collection or supply of evidence in the requested countries for settlement of criminal cases in Vietnam;

d) Examination of criminal liability of persons who are staying in the countries of which they bear the nationality;
dd) Other cases prescribed by Vietnamese law.

