2. Requests for criminal legal assistance from foreign countries must be made in the form of criminal legal mandate under the provisions of this Law.

Article 21. Refusal or postponement of execution of criminal legal mandates of foreign

countries
1. A foreign criminal legal mandate shall be rejected in the following cases:

a) It does not conform to treaties to which Vietnam is a member or to Vietnamese law;
b) It causes harm to national sovereignty or security;

c) It is related to the criminal prosecution of a person for his/her criminal act for which he/she was sentenced, declared unguilty or granted general or special amnesty in Vietnam;
d) It is related to criminal acts for which the statute of limitations of criminal prosecution has expired under the provisions of Criminal Code of Vietnam;

dd) It is related to a violation against laws; however, do not constitute a crime under the provisions of Criminal Code of Vietnam.

2. The execution of criminal legal mandates may be postponed in Vietnam if it obstructs the process of investigation, prosecution, trial or judgment enforcement in Vietnam.
3. When deciding to refuse or postpone the execution of criminal legal mandates in accordance with Clauses 1 and 2 of this Article, the Supreme People’s Procuracy shall send a notice to the requesting countries, providing the explanation and measures to be applied.

Article 22. Procedures for criminal legal mandates to foreign countries

1. Presiding authorities in Vietnam requesting overseas competent authorities to provide criminal legal assistance shall prepare a legal mandate requests as stipulated in Article 18 of this Law and send them to the Supreme People’s Procuracy.

