3. Presiding authorities of Vietnam that refuse extradition in accordance with Clauses 1 and 2 hereof shall notify competent authorities in the extradition-requesting countries thereof.

Article 36. Extradition requests

1. An extradition request must include:
a) A written extradition request of the competent authority;

b) Documents as prescribed in Article 37 of this Law.
2. The extradition request shall be made in three sets in accordance with this Law and the law of the requesting country. Language used in the request complies with Article 5 of this Law.

Article 37. Written extradition requests and enclosed documents

1. A written extradition request must include:

a) Date, month, year and place of issuance;
b) Reason for the extradition request;

c) Name and address of the competent authority requesting the extradition;
d) Name and address of the authority requested to effect the extradition;

dd) Full name, gender, birth date, nationality, residence place of, and other necessary information on, the person requested for extradition.
2. A written extradition request must be enclosed with the following documents:

a) Summarized content of the case;

b) Legal provisions applicable for the determination of factors constituting the crime and name of the crime, the provisions on penalties, the statute of limitations for criminal prosecution or the statute of limitations for enforcement of penalties against that crime;
c) Papers on the nationality and place of residence of the person requested for extradition, if any;

d) Other documents describing the identity and photos of the person requested for extradition as required by international law and practice.

