Article 39. Consideration of extradition requests from multiple countries for one person

1. In the case where the Ministry of Public Security receives written requests from two or more countries for the extradition of one person for the same crime or many different crimes, the Ministry of Public Security shall take charge and cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Ministry of Justice, the Supreme People’s Procuracy and the Supreme People’s Court in considering and deciding to execute the extradition request of one of the requesting countries and transfer the extradition requests to the concerned regional People’s Court for extradition consideration and decision.
2. Upon consideration of extradition requests prescribed in Clause 1 of this Article, in addition to legal provisions, the following relevant factors must also be considered:

a) The effectual nationality and last place of residence of the person requested for extradition;

b) The legitimacy and compatibility of the extradition request;
c) Time and place of crime commission;

d) Specific interests of the requesting countries;
dd) The severity of the crime;

e) The nationality of the victim;

g) Possibility of subsequent extradition between the requesting countries;

h) Date of the extradition request;
i) Other relevant factors.

