3. The regional People’s Court shall consider an extradition request within 30 days, from the date on which the decision is issued in accordance with point a Clause 2 of this Article and send a set of the request to the People’s Procuracy of the same level.
4. The extradition request shall be considered at sessions of a council consisting of three judges, including a presiding judge, with the participation of members of the People’s Procuracy of the same level.

The extradition request-considering council shall follow the order:

a) A council member presents the contents of the extradition requests and states his/her opinions on the legal grounds of the extradition;

b) The procurator states the viewpoints of the People’s Procuracy;
c) The lawyer or lawful representative of the person requested for extradition presents his/her opinions, if any;

d) The person requested for extradition states his/her opinions;
dd) Based on the provisions of this Law, relevant provisions of other Vietnamese laws and treaties to which Vietnam is a member, the council discusses and decides by majority on the extradition or extradition refusal.

5. Within 10 working days from the date on which the decision on extradition or extradition refusal is issued, the regional People’s Court shall send such decision to the person requested for extradition, the People’s Procuracy of the same level and the Ministry of Public Security for the exercise of rights and performance of obligations according to law.
The person requested for extradition may appeal and the People’s Procuracy of the same level may protest within fifteen days, the People’s Procuracy may protest within thirty days as from the date the regional People’s Court issues decisions. The regional People’s Court shall forward the requests, appeals and protests to the Supreme People’s Court within seven days from the date the appeal or protest time limit expires.

