1. A person serving imprisonment sentences overseas may be received back to Vietnam for enforcement of imprisonment sentences when the following conditions are fully met:
a) He/she is a Vietnamese citizen;

b) He/she has the last place of residence in Vietnam;
c) The offense for which he/she was convicted abroad also constitutes a crime under Vietnamese laws;

d) By the time of receiving the transfer requests, the remaining duration of serving the imprisonment sentences must be at least one year; in special cases, this duration must be at least six months;

dd) The judgment against the person to be transferred must be legally effective and there are no pending legal proceedings against him/her in the transferring country;
e) The transfer has the consent of the transferring country;

g) The transfer has the consent of the person to be transferred.
2. A person serving imprisonment sentences in Vietnam may be transferred to a foreign country for enforcement of imprisonment sentences when the following conditions are fully met:

a) He/she is citizen of the receiving country or is the person permitted to reside indefinitely or having relatives in the receiving country;
b) He/she fully satisfies the conditions specified in points c, d, dd, e, and g Clause 1 of this Article and has fulfilled his/her civil responsibilities and additional penalties such as fines, property confiscation and other legal responsibilities in the judgments;

c) The transfer has the consent of the receiving country;

Article 51. Refusal to transfer persons serving imprisonment sentences

The competent authority of Vietnam shall refuse to transfer persons serving imprisonment sentences in Vietnam to foreign countries in the following cases:

1. When they have grounds to believe that the person to be transferred may be tortured, retaliated or oppressed in the receiving countries;
2. The transfer may harm the national sovereignty or security of Vietnam.

Article 52. Requests for transfer persons serving imprisonment sentences

