5. Within 10 working days from the date on which the decision on transfer or transfer refusal is issued, the regional People’s Court shall send such decision to the person requested for transfer, the People’s Procuracy of the same level and the Ministry of Public Security for the exercise of rights and performance of obligations according to law.

The person requested for transfer may appeal and the People’s Procuracy of the same level may protest within fifteen days, the People’s Procuracy may protest within thirty days as from the date the regional People’s Court issues decisions. The regional People’s Court shall forward the requests, appeals and protests to the Supreme People’s Court within seven days from the date the appeal or protest time limit expires.

Within 20 days after receiving the transfer requests and appeals or protests, the regional People’s Court shall open a court session for appealed or protested decision consideration; the appellate council shall decide on the transfer or transfer refusal. The order for examination of appeals or protests against transfer decisions of regional People’s Courts shall comply with Clause 4 of this Article.
